# The A5 refresh workflow caches a verified upstream Git mirror and enforces
# regeneration from this revision. Raw Smithy models are not vendored; only the
# compact generated manifest and the pruned shape snapshot are committed.
#
# shapes-sha256 covers the whole models/aws/shapes/ directory: sha256 over the
# bytewise-sorted `<sha256-of-file>  <relative-path>` lines. Reproduce it with
# `cd models/aws/shapes && sha256sum -t *.json | LC_ALL=C sort | sha256sum -t`
# (-t forces text mode, which is already the default outside Windows).
# The snapshot is a generated derivative of the pinned models, generator input
# only, never read at runtime — see cmd/awsmodelgen/README.md and
# docs/plans/inert-tier-rollout.md §4.6.
#
# sdk-shapes-sha256 covers the generated tables in internal/awsshapes/ (its
# index.gen.go and every tables/*.txt) with the same definition: reproduce it with
# `cd internal/awsshapes && sha256sum -t index.gen.go tables/*.txt | LC_ALL=C sort | sha256sum -t`.
# Those tables are packed into the binary by `make aws-sdk-shapes` and decoded
# lazily for Step Functions' aws-sdk integrations; models/aws/sdk-shapes-services.txt
# lists their services.
